--- NOTE on the HTTP limit test's window (not part of the finding, required by the gate) ---
The first instrumented gate run of this task failed "A connection that sends a partial request and stalls is
dropped" at `server.connectionCount == 1`: this task changes no Swift, so it is the same load-sensitivity the
A157 probes had. The test polls the main actor for the registered connection while the idle deadline is one
second, and a busy instrumented gate can keep the poll off the actor past that deadline — so a registration
that happened is reported as one that never did. The deadline the test drives is three seconds now, which
keeps the race out of the *observation* without touching either assertion: the connection still has to be
accepted, and it still has to be reaped with a 408. Three consecutive runs pass in 3.2 s each.

